SUMMARY:Dynamical Tidal Response of Neutron Stars from Scattering Amplitudes
DESCRIPTION:Séminaire Amplitudes et Gravitation sur l'Yvette (IHES/IPhT) In this talk I will describe an amplitude-based framework for extracting the frequency-dependent tidal response of neutron stars while preserving the tidal resonances associated with their normal modes. The response is obtained by matching the amplitude for gravitational-wave scattering off a neutron star\, equivalently gravitational Comp\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/17400/
